      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean i get the warning but i actually read an article saying that high doses of vit c can help with kidney health by supporting the renal system. i'm not looking to do anything crazy, just thinking like maybe 1500mg or 2000mg would be a safe sweet spot to try for a few weeks to see if it helps. if i'm drinking plenty of water like you said, isn't that basically neutralizing any risk? it feels like i shouldn't be afraid to try something that's literally just a vitamin.",
